tangle in its grid. The program below is that check: it runs on all train pairs, and any mismatch would point to the problem.\n\n**Test input.** The obvious candidate is the large 0 region around rows 12–16, cols 10–15. The program finds the maximal all‑0 rectangle itself rather than assuming this one.\n\n**Assumptions.**\n- The block colour 0 and the fill colour 8 are the same in every pair, so I use them as constants.\n- If two rectangles tie for largest, the program keeps the first one found in scan order.\n\nThe search is brute force with prefix sums over every rectangle. That is fine for grids up to 30×30.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    z = (g == 0).astype(int)\n    P = np.zeros((H + 1, W + 1), int)\n    P[1:, 1:] = z.cumsum(0).cumsum(1)\n    best = None\n    bestA = 0\n    for y0 in range(H):\n        for y1 in range(y0 + 2, H):\n            for x0 in range(W):\n                for x1 in range(x0 + 2, W):\n                    a = (y1 - y0 + 1) * (x1 - x0 + 1)\n                    if a <= bestA:\n                        continue\n                    s = P[y1 + 1, x1 + 1] - P[y0, x1 + 1] - P[y1 + 1, x0] + P[y0, x0]\n                    if s == a:\n                        bestA = a\n                        best = (y0, x0, y1, x1)\n    out = g.copy()\n    if best:\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = best\n        out[y0 + 1:y1, x0 + 1:x1] = 8\n        emit(out, f\"Largest all-0 rectangle is rows {y0}-{y1}, cols {x0}-{x1}; \"\n                  f\"keep its 1-cell 0 border and fill the interior with 8.\")\n    else:\n        emit(out, \"No all-0 rectangle large enough to have an interior; grid unchanged.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Find the largest‑area axis‑aligned rectangle made only of 0s."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"I have not run a separate check that each of these blocks is the largest all‑0 rectangle in its grid."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- If two rectangles tie for largest, the program keeps the first one found in scan order."}],"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Each pair takes the input and recolours one solid block of black (0) cells to 8."}],"movement":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Find the largest‑area axis‑aligned rectangle made only of 0s."}],"topology":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Largest all-0 rectangle is rows 3-6, cols 5-8; keep its 1-cell 0 border and fill the interior with 8."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Largest all-0 rectangle is rows 4-9, cols 4-8; keep its 1-cell 0 border and fill the interior with 8."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Largest all-0 rectangle is rows 10-13, cols 7-12; keep its 1-cell 0 border and fill the interior with 8."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"0b5b3ab82ff419e4d162ac46eb24f42577a63983c734130511b8818b50c670ab","task_sha256":"c3a16e947d0bb29ff20255911fe2a88d39ecb2e3d73011ee10e0fe17d0ef0196","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
